-- More of what works today, as the code reads it: the on/off stats ("Cannot be Knocked Back": a quantity that is
-- on while the stat is not 0) and the stats that are a property of their own item (local_: its armour, its sockets,
-- its attack speed), worked out when the item's own numbers are. target item_self marks the second kind, and their
-- fx_stats rows become handled 'item'. Nothing reads these rows; they record what happens and stay unchecked.
ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
ON CONFLICT(stat, ord) DO NOTHING;
ON CONFLICT(stat, ord) DO NOTHING;
